SELECT eos.consume_idempotent();            -- balance 175
SELECT eos.simulate_lost_ack(0);
SELECT eos.consume_idempotent();            -- still 175
SELECT balance_cents, last_offset FROM eos.accounts WHERE account_id = 'alice';
```

Write-up: `simulate_lost_ack` is at-least-once redelivery after a lost ack. `consume_idempotent` stores the message offset on the sink row and skips already-applied offsets — the book’s "include the offset with the value" pattern. Advancing `consumer_offset` in the same function/transaction as the guarded update is the atomic-commit idea for side effect + ack. A production stream runtime still needs fencing so a zombie consumer cannot write concurrently, and deterministic ordered replay from the log.
